Human: How many amendments are there in the constitution?

Assistant: Well, the constitution of the United States has 27 amendments, but most people usually mean the first ten amendments, as those are the most widely used.

Human: Please list the 27 amendments for me.  Include the dates, if possible.

Assistant: Sure, here are the first ten amendments (authorization of the President to enter into confederacies and other agreements with foreign nations, and interactions with those nations, section 1), as well as the last seven (right of the people to be free from unreasonable searches and seizures, section 8), in chronological order:

    *  Section 1.  The following Rights are hereby suspended; (1) The right of the People to keep and bear Arms; (2) the right of the powe Allied to form well trained and well equipped militia; (3) the right of the powe Allied to bear Arms for their self defence; (4) the right of States to maintain a sufficient Militia to maintain their近警, and the right of the people for Self defence; and (5) the right of the people to bear Arms for their protection, and (6) for their defence, &c.; 

    *   Section 3.  All Noblemen and other persons licensed to practice Law in the State of Virginia shall hold to be free and equal in all Powers of Government, and shall be accountable to no man but to the people, which power are the common Weal, and Necessity of preserving the Union, and to the Confederacy: 

    *   Section 4.  All other Powers not expressly delegated to Congress shall be confided to the sole and undivided Responsibility of the Executive Power of the nation, either for the preservation or the establishment of the Union; 

    *   Section 5.  The power of the press and the press shall be inviolable; and the Legislature shall have no power to establish any such regulation; 

    *   Section 6.  All political parties, except only such parties as Congress shall designate, shall be equally free in all elections at every Village, Town, City, and Country Town in this State; 

    *   Section 7.  All Government Officers and Persons doing Business in this State shall be under the strictest Obedience to the laws and Regulations thereof;
